.TH HD-NETWORK 7 "October 2026" "hd-network" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-network \- the hyprdebian network configuration
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B hd-network
renders the
.BR systemd-networkd (8)
files in
.I /etc/systemd/network
from the key
.B hd-network
in the hyprdebian configuration,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ,
with
.BR hd-network-render (8).
The settings are changed with
.BR hd-network-iface (8)
for wired and wifi interfaces and
.BR hd-network-bridge (8)
for bridges.
They read the settings, check the change and write the result with
.BR hd-config-update (8);
see
.BR hd-config (7).
.PP
Installing the package configures nothing: it does not set the key, and it
does not run
.BR hd-network-render .
.PP
The package also installs
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/10-ethernet.link
and
.IR 20-wifi.link ,
which name ethernet and wifi interfaces by their path, such as
.B enp3s0
and
.BR wlp2s0 ,
and give them a persistent MAC address.
A file with the same name in
.I /etc/systemd/network
takes their place.
.SH SETTINGS
The key
.B hd-network
holds a JSON object with these fields, all optional:
.TP
.B interfaces
An object that maps interface names to their settings.
The name may be a glob, such as
.BR en* ;
an interface whose exact name is listed uses its own settings, not those
of a glob.
Interfaces that are not listed are left alone by systemd-networkd.
.TP
.B bridges
An object that maps bridge names to their settings.
.TP
.B wait_online
.B false
masks
.BR systemd-networkd-wait-online.service ,
so the boot does not wait for the network;
.B true
unmasks it.
Left out, the service is left as it is.
.PP
An interface with the field
.B bridge
is a port of that bridge, which must be in
.BR bridges .
It has no other fields and no addresses of its own.
A wifi interface, one whose name starts with
.BR wl ,
cannot be a port.
.PP
Every other interface, and every bridge, has these fields, all optional:
.TP
.B dhcp
.B true
(the default) gets addresses with DHCPv4 and with IPv6 router
advertisements and DHCPv6, and uses the search domains they hand out.
.B false
turns all three off.
.TP
.B addresses
Static addresses with their prefix length, IPv4 and IPv6 mixed, such as
.BR 192.168.1.10/24 .
A string or a list.
They may be combined with DHCP.
.TP
.B gateway
The default gateway, or a list with one for IPv4 and one for IPv6.
.TP
.B dns
DNS servers, a string or a list.
.TP
.B metric
The metric of the routes, from DHCP and to the gateways.
The default is 100; the route with the lowest metric wins, so give wifi a
higher one than ethernet.
.PP
A bridge also has the field
.BR mac ,
its MAC address.
.B hd-network-bridge
gives a new bridge a random, locally administered address, and
.B hd-network-render
does the same for a bridge without one.
The address is stored in the settings, so it never changes, also not when
the machine-id changes.
.PP
Unknown fields are errors, so typing mistakes are caught.
.SH EXAMPLES
DHCP on every ethernet interface, and on the wifi interface with a higher
metric:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hd-network-iface set 'en*'
hd-network-iface set wlp2s0 \-\-metric 200
hd-network-render
.fi
.RE
.PP
This gives these settings:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
    "interfaces": {
        "en*": {},
        "wlp2s0": { "metric": 200 }
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
A bridge for virtual machines, with enp3s0 as its port and DHCP on the
bridge:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hd-network-bridge set br0
hd-network-iface set enp3s0 \-\-bridge br0
.fi
.RE
.PP
which gives:
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
    "interfaces": {
        "enp3s0": { "bridge": "br0" }
    },
    "bridges": {
        "br0": { "mac": "52:54:00:3a:1f:c2" }
    }
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
A static address:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hd-network-iface set enp3s0 \-\-no\-dhcp \e
    \-\-address 192.168.1.10/24 \-\-address fd00::10/64 \e
    \-\-gateway 192.168.1.1 \-\-gateway fd00::1 \-\-dns 192.168.1.1
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration, with the settings under the key
.BR hd-network .
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/network
Where the files are rendered.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hd-network/templates
The jinja2 templates the files are made from.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/hd-network/hd_network.py
The code that hd-network-render, hd-network-iface and hd-network-bridge
share: reading, checking and writing the settings.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/10-ethernet.link
.TQ
.I /usr/lib/systemd/network/20-wifi.link
Name ethernet and wifi interfaces by their path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-network-iface (8),
.BR hd-network-bridge (8),
.BR hd-network-render (8),
.BR hd-config (7),
.BR hd-config-update (8),
.BR systemd.network (5),
.BR systemd.netdev (5),
.BR systemd.link (5)
